WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, obviously,
"The President Show,"

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was a show I adored.
-I did too.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:06.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
It's sadly not coming back.

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:08.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you miss it?
Do you want a --

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:09.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you want to,
in the moment now --

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:12.312
I could just throw you out
a few press conference questions

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:14.414
and get a little Trump from you?
Would you mind that?

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We could improvise
a little bit, sure.

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:17.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How do you feel?
Are you worried today

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:20.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the indictment
of Michael Cohen

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
that this could
lead back to you now?

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:24.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, he specifically
named you in court.

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:29.095
-No, Michael -- First off,
Individual 1 isn't me, okay?

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's an individual,
and he's one guy.

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:34.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's one guy.
We don't know who he is.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.036 line:92%
And Michael was talking to him.

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:38.338 size:84% position:42%
I don't know who he is.
I'll never know him.

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:39.739 line:92%
I'll never know Individual 1.

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:43.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
No matter how hard
I stare into the mirror,

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:44.544 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I'll never know him.

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:46.246 line:92%
I'll never really know him.

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:48.048 line:92%
Melania says she knows him.

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:51.651
What's the next question?
-The next question is --

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:52.852 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Come on. Let's go.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:55.388 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:58.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Obviously,
I don't need to tell you this,

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:00.794
but Democrats
took back control of the House.

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:03.463 size:81% position:41%
And now, you know --
-Excuse me, excuse me.

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:06.666 size:75% position:38%
They took the House.
We took the Senate.

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:08.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And I told Chuck,

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.103 line:92%
and I told Nancy the other day,

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they were at me
from both sides!

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:15.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
They were spit-roasting me
with questions.

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
And --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:19.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
And --
-Well, I would just say,

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, if I could,
Mr. President,

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:23.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
you say you took the Senate.
You had the Senate.

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:26.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I had the Senate,
and I took it back.

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:27.287 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:28.121 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-You lost the House.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:29.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
You had the House.
You lost the House.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:34.260
-I never really lost the House,
because the House always wins.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.497
[ Laughter ]
And we know that from a casino.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:41.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
We know it from "Casino,"
the great Joe Pesci.

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:42.302 line:92%
He gets put in that ditch.

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's gonna happen
to Don Jr.

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
if he messes up,
I'll tell you that.

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:48.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll tell you that.
-Can I throw out some names

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:50.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
of some potential
2020 opponents, maybe?

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You can give me
anybody you want.

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:52.345 size:84% position:42% line:92%
They're all gonna lose.

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:55.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
And even if I lose, I promise
you, I will not concede.

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:58.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
What about Beto O'Rourke?

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:00.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of people are talking
about Beto O'Rourke.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Beto. Beto!
Guy's a Beto male.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:04.624 size:84% position:42% line:92%
He's a total Beto male!

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:10.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's a lanky guy,
and he's big old neck apple.

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:13.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know that neck apple?
-Yeah.

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:14.234 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-The neck apple.

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:17.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Eve took a bite
from the neck apple,

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then
the whole thing was screwed,

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
so we can't have that guy.
He's a snake.

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:23.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Elizabeth War--
Elizabeth Warren?

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:26.880 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Pocahonta-s-s-s-s.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.982 line:92%
Elizabeth Warren took the bait.

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know.
Let me tell you,

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:33.853
I know a good guy named Anthony
from Massachusetts

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:37.323
who would say, "Never let
someone from Massachusetts

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:39.058 size:88% position:44% line:92%
run for president, ever.

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:41.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
Doesn't anyone
remember Dukakis?"

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:44.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
Dukakis.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:45.732 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Exactly.

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:48.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What about Cory Booker.
-Book 'em, Danno!

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:51.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let me tell you
about Cory Booker.

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:53.540 line:92%
Guy's bald, big bald guy.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he likes the ladies.
We all know that.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:56.442 size:75% position:38% line:92%
He likes the ladies.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:03:00.213
Booker, he's got a big mouth,
and he used to jump over the --

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:04.551
He used to drive a car --
T.J. Booker, tough guy.

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:05.084 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
T.J. Booker.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:08.788
And that guy totally resurrected
his career from "Star Trek."

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:12.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
So unbelievable.
-Oh, my God.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:14.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's fantastic.
Fantastic.

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:16.696 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:18.831 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:21.267 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's frightening.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Every now and then,
someone would say to me,

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:27.774
"Hey, would you want to have
the president on this show?"

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:30.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the thing I would say is,
it wouldn't matter.

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:31.644 line:92%
There's this idea that there's

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:32.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
a good interview
out there with him

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:35.348
where he'll actually answer
the questions that are asked.

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:38.351
Would you ever, though,
like to, as him, interview him?

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:40.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think
that you could maybe --

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:41.087 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:42.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
I've never thought I --

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:45.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess, on my show,
we had this same question.

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:48.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
And mind you, he was never
gonna come to our show.

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:52.365
-Sure, right.
-But we did have Deepak Chopra.

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:54.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, the point being --
[ Laughs ]

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:58.705
The point being, I don't think
the value in interviewing him

00:03:58.705 --> 00:04:01.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
is only for
your own benefit, right?

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:02.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, for your own
humor benefit.

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:04.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're not gonna
get information from him.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're not
gonna get anything new.

00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:07.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And, to me, you just

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:12.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
serve a platform
for him to peacock more.

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:18.725
And I think that the greatest or
most bizarre thing

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:20.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that we're still,
three years in,

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:23.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
trying to calculate
what the pieces

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:24.530 line:92%
that were missing about him,

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
especially in the media
and his coverage,

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:29.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's like,
"There is no 'there' there."

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:30.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
I might have said this before
but it's, like,

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:34.907
this is Chauncey Gardiner, like,
times a thousand,

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:37.777 line:92%
which is from "Being There."

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:39.212 line:92%
-Put it on with your Steely Dan.

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:40.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Put it on
with your Steely Dan"!

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:44.884
And then get a rotary telephone
and call your grandmother.

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:46.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I just don't think
there's any value,

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:49.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think that the thing is,
you know, like a tumor,

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:52.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
which our President
is a tumor on democracy,

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:54.360 line:92%
we need to cut the oxygen off.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.830
And the way you cut the oxygen
off is stop focusing on him.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:58.398 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:58.398 --> 00:05:01.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's so many
important things --

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:03.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's so many things
that are important

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:07.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
that both sides
need to deal with.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:09.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, especially,
I speak to the left, which is,

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:12.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
we need to think about
the issues that aren't as sexy

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:16.749
as sort of like the marquee
things of taking down Trump.

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:18.017 line:92%
Tort reform, for instance.

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:19.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know no one wants
to talk about it,

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:22.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
but people's rights in court
are being taken away

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:23.790 line:92%
by corporations every day,

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we have Amazon
moving to New York very soon,

00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:28.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
and arbitration
is the name of the game

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:30.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
when it comes to trying
to sue a business for money.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
These are real things
that affect people, right?

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:36.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
How we employ people,
keeping children in prison.

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:38.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
Those things matter,
and they're not interesting,

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:40.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they don't stay
on the bill every day.

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:43.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
And prosecuting the president
over a long-form period

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:45.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
on cable news
isn't gonna do anything.

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:47.680 size:78% position:39%
But we can do things
every day that matter

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:50.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
by changing our behavior
and how we interact

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:51.117 line:92%
with people in our lives.

00:05:51.117 --> 00:05:54.087
That's more important than
interviewing the president.

00:05:54.087 --> 00:05:55.955 line:92%
-Well, couldn't agree more.

00:05:55.955 --> 00:05:57.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
And thank you for being here,
buddy.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:00.693
It is always
just such a pleasure to see you.

00:06:00.693 --> 00:06:04.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much.
-Anthony Atamanuik, everybody.

